From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: libipa: add a camera sensor helper for the GC2145

The PinePhone front camera is a GalaxyCore GC2145, driven through the
simple pipeline and the software ISP. Without a helper the IPA cannot turn
a gain code into a gain, so its exposure loop has nothing to work with.

The driver hands the sensor's global gain register straight to userspace:

  drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
    #define GC2145_P0_GLOBAL_GAIN      0xb0
    #define GC2145_GLOBAL_GAIN_UNITY   0x40
    ctrls->a_gain = v4l2_ctrl_new_std(hdl, ops, V4L2_CID_ANALOGUE_GAIN,
                                      GC2145_GLOBAL_GAIN_UNITY, 255, 1,
                                      GC2145_GLOBAL_GAIN_DEFAULT);

so the code is linear with 0x40 as unity - the same shape as the GC02M2
helper, and a divisor of 64 describes it. The pre and post gains belong to
the sensor's own AEC and are not part of this control.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
@@ -520,6 +520,23 @@
 };
 REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("gc08a3", CameraSensorHelperGc08a3)
 
+class CameraSensorHelperGc2145 : public CameraSensorHelper
+{
+public:
+	CameraSensorHelperGc2145()
+	{
+		/*
+		 * The driver exposes the sensor's global gain register
+		 * (0xb0) directly as V4L2_CID_ANALOGUE_GAIN, with 0x40 as
+		 * unity and a range of 0x40..0xff, so the code is linear in
+		 * 1/64 steps. The pre and post gains are the AEC's and are
+		 * not part of this control.
+		 */
+		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 1, 0, 0, 64 };
+	}
+};
+REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("gc2145", CameraSensorHelperGc2145)
+
 class CameraSensorHelperHm1246 : public CameraSensorHelper
 {
 public:
